# HR360 — Process Flow Diagrams

**Document ID:** HR360-BA-006
**Version:** 1.0
**Status:** Draft for Review
**Date:** 20 September 2026
**Prepared By:** Nida Khan
**Role:** Business Analyst / Developer / Project Manager / Scrum Master
**Product Owner:** HR Business Stakeholder

---

## 1. Purpose

This document defines the logical process flows for the HR360 Human Resource Management and Analytics System.

The flows provide a controlled business-analysis reference for:

* Process understanding
* Functional requirements
* User stories
* Acceptance criteria
* API design
* Database design
* Testing and UAT
* Frontend workflow design
* Analytics and reporting

---

## 2. Flow Notation

| Notation      | Meaning                                                             |
| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| START         | Beginning of process                                                |
| Activity      | Business or system action                                           |
| Decision      | Business rule or validation decision                                |
| System        | HR360 application/API/database action                               |
| Business User | Action performed by HR, manager, recruiter or other authorized user |
| END           | Completion of process                                               |

---

# 3. Employee Management Flow

```text
START
  ↓
HR User selects Employee Management
  ↓
Create / View / Update Employee
  ↓
Validate Employee Data
  ↓
Valid?
 ├── NO → Return Validation Error → END
 └── YES
        ↓
Save Employee Record
        ↓
Assign Department
        ↓
Assign Job Role
        ↓
Assign Work Status
        ↓
Assign Employment Status
        ↓
Employee Available in HR360
        ↓
END
```

---

# 4. Employee Lifecycle Flow

```text
START
  ↓
Employee Record
  ↓
Lifecycle Event
  ↓
Update Employment Status
  ↓
Validate Status
  ↓
Valid?
 ├── NO → Return Error → END
 └── YES
        ↓
Persist Status Change
        ↓
Refresh Relevant Analytics
        ↓
END
```

Supported lifecycle states include:

* CANDIDATE
* PROBATION
* EMPLOYED
* ON_LEAVE
* RESIGNED
* TERMINATED
* RETIRED

---

# 5. Department-Specific Active Status Flow

```text
START
  ↓
Employee Record
  ↓
Identify Department
  ↓
Is Department HR?
 ├── YES → employment_status = EMPLOYED?
 │              ├── YES → ACTIVE
 │              └── NO → NOT ACTIVE
 │
 └── NO
       ↓
Is Department Operations?
 ├── YES → work_status = WORKING or ONLINE?
 │              ├── YES → ACTIVE
 │              └── NO → NOT ACTIVE
 │
 └── NO
       ↓
Is Department Finance?
 ├── YES → salary_status = PAID?
 │              ├── YES → ACTIVE
 │              └── NO → NOT ACTIVE
 │
 └── NO → NOT ACTIVE
```

The active status is derived from business rules and is not a universal manually maintained employee status.

---

# 6. Attendance Management Flow

```text
START
  ↓
Select Employee
  ↓
Select Attendance Date
  ↓
Enter Attendance Status
  ↓
Enter Check-in / Check-out
  ↓
Enter Remarks if Required
  ↓
Validate Attendance Data
  ↓
Valid?
 ├── NO → Validation Error → END
 └── YES
        ↓
Save Attendance
        ↓
Calculate / Store Working Hours
        ↓
Attendance Analytics
        ↓
END
```

Supported statuses:

* PRESENT
* ABSENT
* LATE
* HALF_DAY
* ON_LEAVE
* HOLIDAY

---

# 7. Leave Management Flow

```text
START
  ↓
Employee
  ↓
Select Leave Type
  ↓
Enter Start Date / End Date
  ↓
Enter Reason
  ↓
Validate Request
  ↓
Submit Request
  ↓
Approver Reviews Request
  ↓
Approved?
 ├── NO → REJECTED → END
 └── YES → APPROVED
             ↓
        Update Leave Records
             ↓
        Reporting / Analytics
             ↓
            END
```

---

# 8. Performance Review Flow

```text
START
  ↓
Manager / HR
  ↓
Select Employee
  ↓
Define Review Period
  ↓
Enter Rating
  ↓
Enter Feedback
  ↓
Validate Rating
  ↓
Valid Rating 1–5?
 ├── NO → Validation Error → END
 └── YES
        ↓
Save Performance Review
        ↓
Performance Analytics
        ↓
END
```

---

# 9. Performance Improvement Plan Flow

```text
START
  ↓
Performance Concern Identified
  ↓
Manager / HR Creates PIP
  ↓
Define Start Date
  ↓
Define End Date
  ↓
Define Review Cadence
  ↓
PIP Active
  ↓
Periodic Review
  ↓
Progress Evaluation
  ↓
Progress Satisfactory?
 ├── YES → Complete PIP → END
 └── NO
       ↓
Continue / Extend PIP
       ↓
Next Review
```

---

# 10. Training Management Flow

```text
START
  ↓
Create Training Program
  ↓
Select Employee
  ↓
Enroll Employee
  ↓
Record Attendance
  ↓
Training Completed?
 ├── NO → Continue Training
 └── YES
        ↓
Record Completion
        ↓
Record Score
        ↓
Certificate Issued?
        ↓
Update Employee Training Record
        ↓
Training Analytics
        ↓
END
```

---

# 11. Recruitment Pipeline Flow

```text
START
  ↓
Candidate Created
  ↓
Application Created
  ↓
Screening
  ↓
Shortlisted?
 ├── NO → REJECTED / WITHDRAWN → END
 └── YES
        ↓
Interview
        ↓
Interview Result
        ↓
PASS?
 ├── NO → REJECTED → END
 └── YES
        ↓
Job Offer
        ↓
Candidate Decision
        ↓
Accepted?
 ├── NO → DECLINED → END
 └── YES
        ↓
Joining Process
        ↓
Employee Creation
        ↓
END
```

---

# 12. Interview Management Flow

```text
START
  ↓
Select Application
  ↓
Schedule Interview
  ↓
Assign Interviewer
  ↓
Define Interview Round
  ↓
Conduct Interview
  ↓
Record Rating
  ↓
Record Feedback
  ↓
Record Result
  ↓
PASS / FAIL / PENDING
  ↓
Update Application Pipeline
  ↓
END
```

---

# 13. Job Offer Flow

```text
START
  ↓
Eligible Application
  ↓
Create Offer
  ↓
Validate Salary and Dates
  ↓
Offer Valid?
 ├── NO → Validation Error → END
 └── YES
        ↓
Send Offer
        ↓
Candidate Decision
        ↓
Accepted?
 ├── YES → ACCEPTED → Joining Process
 └── NO
       ↓
DECLINED / EXPIRED / CANCELLED
       ↓
END
```

---

# 14. Recruitment-to-Employee Transition

```text
Candidate
   ↓
Application
   ↓
Screening
   ↓
Interview
   ↓
Offer
   ↓
Offer Accepted
   ↓
Joining Date
   ↓
Employee Record
   ↓
Department Assignment
   ↓
Role Assignment
   ↓
Work Status
   ↓
Employment Status
   ↓
Employee Available in HR360
```

This is a target-state process and will be further refined during frontend and onboarding design.

