---

# 16. API Request Lifecycle

```text
Client / Frontend
      ↓
REST API Endpoint
      ↓
Request Validation
      ↓
Business / Data Operation
      ↓
PostgreSQL
      ↓
Success?
 ├── NO → Controlled Error Response
 └── YES → Structured JSON Response
      ↓
Frontend / Consumer
```

---

# 17. Key Business Decision Rules

| Decision                 | Condition                      | Outcome               |
| ------------------------ | ------------------------------ | --------------------- |
| HR Active Status         | HR + EMPLOYED                  | ACTIVE                |
| HR Non-active            | HR + not EMPLOYED              | NOT ACTIVE            |
| Operations Active Status | Operations + WORKING/ONLINE    | ACTIVE                |
| Operations Non-active    | Operations + other work status | NOT ACTIVE            |
| Finance Active Status    | Finance + salary PAID          | ACTIVE                |
| Finance Non-active       | Finance + salary not PAID      | NOT ACTIVE            |
| Interview Result         | Interview outcome recorded     | PASS / FAIL / PENDING |
| Offer Accepted           | Candidate accepts offer        | ACCEPTED              |
| Offer Declined           | Candidate declines offer       | DECLINED              |
| Leave Approved           | Approver approves request      | APPROVED              |
| Leave Rejected           | Approver rejects request       | REJECTED              |

---

# 18. Exception and Validation Paths

HR360 processes must handle the following conditions:

* Duplicate employee code
* Duplicate email
* Invalid department reference
* Invalid job role reference
* Invalid work status
* Invalid employment status
* Invalid attendance status
* Invalid leave information
* Invalid performance rating
* Invalid interview rating
* Invalid candidate/application status
* Invalid salary values
* Invalid offer dates
* Invalid foreign-key references
* Database failures
* API request validation failures

Errors should be returned through controlled API responses without exposing credentials, database passwords or internal secrets.

---

# 19. Process-to-System Interaction

The target HR360 architecture follows this logical interaction:

```text
Business User
     ↓
HR360 Frontend
     ↓
REST API Layer
     ↓
Business Rules / Validation
     ↓
PostgreSQL Database
     ↓
Analytics APIs
     ↓
HR360 Dashboard / Power BI
```

The backend REST APIs and PostgreSQL database are already established in the current implementation. The frontend and Power BI layers are planned project components.

